-- title:
--   The exact logarithm scale table of the q=5 fourth-power construction
-- statement:
--   The exact logarithm scale table of the $q=5$ fourth-power construction, as machine-checkable data.
--
--   Each entry is a pair $(q, k)$ of a positive rational argument and a scale, chosen so that $q\,2^k \ge 1$; entryValid is the Boolean test of exactly that admissibility. The entries are stored in thirty-one chunks and entries is their concatenation, with rgument and scale the two projections at an index.
--
--   The table collects every rational whose natural logarithm the scalar bookkeeping needs, at an accuracy beyond floating point. It stores no logarithm values: the interval endpoints are computed from $q$, $k$ and a term count by the companion auto-scaled interval definition, so nothing here has to be trusted or separately certified.
-- source:
--   Logarithm table for the scalar bookkeeping of the recursive restricted-value construction of Duan, Wu, and Zhou, Faster Matrix Multiplication via Asymmetric Hashing, arXiv:2210.10173v5, Section 7, for the released fourth-power witness.

import Mathlib.Tactic

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option warningAsError true
set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option maxHeartbeats 0

namespace MME.DWZFourthLogScaleTable

def entryValid (entry : Prod Rat Nat) : Bool :=
  decide (0 < entry.1 /\ 1 <= entry.1 * 2 ^ entry.2)

